// [100]  slice 4 (PR  review P1): the Capability Security Pass surfaces the AUTHORITY binding of
// each value-moving leg machine-readably — which participant+role is the authorization actor for which
// effect+ledger — and that surfacing TRACKS the actual binding, so a leg silently rebound to the WRONG
// declared participant is DETECTED (surfaced), not hidden behind the generic "N participants declared"
// count. This is what makes the fields_security_cbi.cmake `Insurer -> reserve_debit` pin a real
// regression guard against a producer+golden co-drift, not a hardcoded string.
//
// POSITIVE: the committed insurance leg names the Insurer authority for the reserve debit.
// RUN: %neutrino-gen --target=security --scenario=%S/Inputs/core_reserve_authority/scenario/core_reserve_authority_happy_path.json %S/Inputs/core_reserve_authority/source/core_reserve_authority.neu -o %t.ok
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=AUTH < %t.ok/security.json
// AUTH: leg 'reserve_debit' (debit insurance.reserve) authorized by participant 'Insurer' (role 'insurer')
//
// NEGATIVE (tamper): rebind reserve_debit to a DIFFERENT declared participant (Customer). The surfacing
// must now name Customer and NOT Insurer for that leg — proving it is binding-faithful, so the wrong
// binding is inspectable and the field pin would fail on such a regression.
// RUN: sed 's/participant     = "Insurer"/participant     = "Customer"/' %S/Inputs/core_reserve_authority/source/core_reserve_authority.neu > %t.mut.neu
// RUN: %neutrino-gen --target=security --scenario=%S/Inputs/core_reserve_authority/scenario/core_reserve_authority_happy_path.json %t.mut.neu -o %t.mut
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MUT < %t.mut/security.json
// MUT: leg 'reserve_debit' (debit insurance.reserve) authorized by participant 'Customer' (role 'customer')
// MUT-NOT: authorized by participant 'Insurer'
